+// CRITICAL-2 + whole-cluster kill -9: an INTERNAL partition (led by the
+// consensus leader) — every node is process-killed and restarted; the consensus
+// first elects the replica that lagged.  It must stay incomplete (no write, no
+// truncation directive) until it proves a pigeonhole quorum; the consensus then
+// moves on and nothing acked is lost.
